# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Max for Live build artifacts
m4l/generated/
# BUILT devices are never published: Max bakes the [js] object's absolute argument
# into the .amxd, so a built device carries the builder's own home directory and
# works on no other machine. The .maxpat SOURCE is tracked and is clean.
m4l/*.amxd

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local logs / scratch
*.log
scratch/

# OUR WORKING DOCS — kept locally, never published.
# Design notes, porting logs, roadmaps and research. Useful to us, useless to a user
# of the bridge, and historically where private paths and personal details collected.
# The public docs are README.md, docs/GUIDE.md, docs/PROTOCOL.md, docs/TOOLS.md and
# docs/LOM_REFERENCE.md.
/DESIGN.md
/PORTING.md
/docs/ROADMAP.md
/docs/COMPARISON.md
/docs/AUDIO_UNDERSTANDING.md
/docs/SIDECAR.md
/docs/LIVE_TEST_PLAN.md
# Compares our tool surface against the fork's — internal, like COMPARISON.md.
/docs/TOOL_OVERVIEW.md
# Draft announcement copy. Publishing the script for promoting something alongside the
# thing itself reads badly, and these are drafts to edit, not documentation.
/docs/LAUNCH.md

# Personal terms for scripts/check_private.py. Kept local ON PURPOSE: a checker that
# hard-codes your private folder names would publish what it is meant to hide.
.private-terms

# SECRETS — never publish. This repo is PUBLIC.
# The .example file IS tracked (it is a template and holds no key).
secrets/
*api_key*.txt
!*api_key*.txt.example
*.key

# Private agent-instruction files — kept LOCAL, never published.
# These guide the AI assistant while developing; they are private workflow and
# irrelevant to the program running. (README.md is public and stays tracked.)
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/

# Gemini review transcripts — may quote source and are not part of the project.
gemini_reviews/

# GEMINI: WHAT SHIPS AND WHAT DOES NOT.
#
# The bridge speaks MCP, so a Claude user already has a window — the Claude desktop app.
# A Gemini user had nothing, because Gemini reaches the bridge through function calling
# rather than MCP. So Gemini Studio SHIPS: it is the second front end, and the reason
# gemini_studio.py, gemini_tools.py, gemini_ui.py and gemini_client.py are all tracked.
#
# What stays local is the DEVELOPMENT tooling — the peer-review chat and the CLI driver.
# They are how this project is built, not part of what anyone installs.
/tools/ask_gemini.py
/tools/gemini_chat.py
/tools/gemini_drive.py
/docs/GEMINI_TOOLS.md
